    "UAE bukan negara Apostille, jadi dokumen Indonesia harus lewat rantai legalisasi lama: Kemenkum, lalu Kemlu, lalu Kedutaan UAE. Stiker Kemenkum adalah syarat sebelum Kemlu.": "The UAE is not an Apostille country, so Indonesian documents must go through the older legalisation chain: Kemenkum, then Kemlu, then the UAE Embassy. The Kemenkum sticker is required before Kemlu.",
    "UAE memakai 230 V 50 Hz colokan tipe G (sumber sekunder). Pengisi daya 100-240 V cukup diberi adaptor.": "The UAE uses 230 V 50 Hz with type G plugs (secondary source). Chargers rated 100-240 V only need an adapter.",
    "UAE tidak menerima Apostille. Urutannya tetap: kampus, Kementerian Hukum, Kemlu, lalu atestasi UAE. Setiap dokumen diproses sendiri-sendiri; dokumen yang dilaminasi ditolak.": "The UAE does not accept Apostille. The order stays fixed: university, Kementerian Hukum, Kemlu, then UAE attestation. Each document is processed separately; laminated documents are rejected.",
    "UU 18/2017 Pasal 5 mensyaratkan kepesertaan jaminan sosial bagi pekerja migran. BPJS Kesehatan juga diminta untuk SKCK.": "UU 18/2017 Article 5 requires migrant workers to be members of social security. BPJS Kesehatan is also required for the SKCK.",
    "UU 18/2017 Pasal 63: pekerja yang bekerja untuk pemberi kerja berbadan hukum tanpa agen wajib melapor ke instansi ketenagakerjaan dan Perwakilan RI. Aturan pelaksananya untuk tenaga profesional belum ditemukan.": "UU 18/2017 Article 63: a worker who works for an incorporated employer without an agent must report to the manpower office and the Indonesian representative office (Perwakilan RI). The implementing rule for professionals has not been found.",
